invariant: INV-26
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: AES=soft stops being one implementation and adds the instructions
  beside it, so a device QUIC object on AES=soft carries two definitions
  of aes_expand_round_keys and aes_cipher_block. The rule is the one PIN
  keeps: one implementation per device object, chosen by a build
  variable, never two; a host object's pair is the one docs/decisions.md
  81 and 89 admit, under names of their own. The linker would refuse this
  particular pair, but a linker is not the gate -- it says nothing about
  which implementation an object ended up with. The lint reads the
  packaged source list per build, so it names the file that does not
  belong.

--- old
AES_IMPL := quic_aes_soft.c
--- new
AES_IMPL := quic_aes_soft.c aes_hw.c
